From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wee8 maintenance <noreply@moonbitlang.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:18:19 +0800
Subject: Reclaim duplicate canonical-type candidates

Upstream-Status: Backport: V8 9423d125979b0fdb466816694e0edcee14c220b6 and 8c9a0bd40d7e290ea19a907400f1b892d63ad5d7
Maintenance: Drop after the pinned V8 contains equivalent ZoneSnapshot and duplicate-candidate rollback. Preserve new canonical types under the canonicalizer mutex.
Tests: store-lifetimes singleton/recursive cases and zone rollback across allocation segments.
Original-Recipe: c755c8163a2702c822eaf875ce52c1d02823e267 patches/wee8-canonical-type-storage.patch

Backport the ZoneSnapshot/Restore approach used by upstream V8:
https://chromium.googlesource.com/v8/v8/+/3dbba7b86bcd7904134a95dd4bebb78579081d95/src/wasm/canonical-types.cc
https://chromium.googlesource.com/v8/v8/+/3dbba7b86bcd7904134a95dd4bebb78579081d95/src/zone/zone.h
https://chromium.googlesource.com/v8/v8/+/3dbba7b86bcd7904134a95dd4bebb78579081d95/src/zone/zone.cc

Keep the pinned ZoneScope's out-of-line constructor/destructor convention.
The canonicalizer mutex covers allocation, lookup and rollback; only duplicate
candidates are discarded. Published canonical representatives remain alive.

